{
  "stage": "write",
  "item": "ch05.s03",
  "inputs_hash": "8a5fd82f7846e8fe4de83ff314ed7fb2a8a923b170ffbe0d815d9fac8cfdad49",
  "output_hash": "44193ada025c0f86c6f3f116390610c94ae069628aa1269e3e5d842eb5224a50",
  "output": {
    "section_id": "ch05.s03",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "ch05.s03.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p01.01",
            "text": "How do the released GPT-2 files tell you what tokens the model knows and what settings the model expects?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p01.02",
            "text": "The file \"encoder.json\" is the vocabulary: it maps tokens to token IDs.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@531",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@537",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@539",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@541",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@547",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@549",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@551"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p01.03",
            "text": "That vocabulary has 50,257 tokens.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@553",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@555",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@558",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@560"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p01.04",
            "text": "Its token IDs start at 0, and the end-of-text token is 50,256.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@555",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@558"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p01.05",
            "text": "The file \"vocab.bpe\" defines byte pair encoding, a subword tokenization scheme.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@562",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@568",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@570",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@573"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p01.06",
            "text": "In this scheme, the encoder looks for pairs of tokens that occur most frequently, merges a pair, and then treats that merged pair as a token.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@573",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@575",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@577",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@579",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@581"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p01.07",
            "text": "The \"vocab.bpe\" file therefore lists merged tokens, with the merges of highest probability appearing at the top of the list.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@586",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@589",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@591",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@593",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@595",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@597",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@599"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p01.08",
            "text": "A special marker shown as \"g-dot\" is an OpenAI convention that indicates one token has ended and a new token has begun.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@601",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@603",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@606",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@608",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@610",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@615",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@617",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@620",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@622"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p01.09",
            "text": "You can think of that marker as a space that marks the beginning of a new token.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@610",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@612",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@615"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s03.p02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p02.01",
            "text": "The release files also record the architectural settings needed to interpret the weights.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p02.02",
            "text": "The file \"hparams.json\" contains the model settings, including vocabulary size, context length, embedding dimension, number of attention heads, and number of transformer blocks.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@622",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@624",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@627",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@629",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@633",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@636",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@662",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@665",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@669",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@671",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@674"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p02.03",
            "text": "For the settings shown here, the vocabulary size is 50,257, the context length is 1,024, and the embedding dimension is 768.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@629",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@631",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@633",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@636"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p02.04",
            "text": "The embedding dimension means that each token ID is converted into a vector in a 768-dimensional space.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@640",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@641",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@643",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@647",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@649",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@651",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@654"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p02.05",
            "text": "The parameter \"n_heads\" is the number of attention heads in each transformer block, and \"n_layer\" is the number of transformer blocks.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@659",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@662",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@665",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@669",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@671",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@674"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p02.06",
            "text": "The values being shown are for the smallest GPT-2 model.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@677",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@680",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@682"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch05.s03.p03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p03.01",
            "text": "When these files are loaded in code, the same setting information is kept in a Python dictionary.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p03.02",
            "text": "The code maintains a dictionary called \"settings\".",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@788",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@790",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@792"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p03.03",
            "text": "This \"settings\" dictionary contains exactly the same information as \"hparams.json\": vocabulary size, context length, embedding dimension, number of attention heads, and number of transformer blocks.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@794",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@796",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@797",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@800",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@802",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@804",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@806",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1658",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1659",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1662",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1664",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1666"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p03.04",
            "text": "If you inspect that dictionary, you see keys such as \"n_vocab\", \"n_ctx\", \"n_embed\", \"n_head\", and \"n_layer\".",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1827",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1829",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1831",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1833",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1835",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1838"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p03.05",
            "text": "Those keys are the \"hparams.json\" information converted into a dictionary.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1841",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1844",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@1847"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch05.s03.p03.06",
            "text": "Downloading the files alone is not enough, because you also need to understand the format in which the returned \"params\" dictionary is stored.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "yXrGeDNuymY@442",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@444",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@447",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@451",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@453",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@455",
              "yXrGeDNuymY@457"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "invalid_citation_sentences": 0
  }
}
